Given Manhattan distance from school to house: D = |x - s_x| + |y - s_y|. A point p lies on some shortest path if dist(school,p) + dist(p,house) = D. That is, p is "on a Manhattan shortest path". Since Manhattan metric, p lies within rectangle with corners school and house, and moving monotone in each coordinate direction: the condition is that p_x is between
